WEBVTT

NOTE "The Envelope". Fair Standard track authored to the Netflix English TTSG.
NOTE Speaker identifiers only where the speaker cannot be seen ([unknown voice]).

c001
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.120
There's one with no name on it.

c002
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.320
No name at all?

c003
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.000
Just the address. Handwritten.

c004
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.300
Then it's mine.

c005
00:00:06.387 --> 00:00:07.720
How is it yours?

c006
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.200
I'm expecting something.

c007
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.300
You're always expecting something.

c008
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.600
Give it here.

c009
00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:14.120
Not until we know.

c010
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.200
-Know what?
-Whose it is. Obviously.

c011
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.400
[unknown voice] Don't open that.

c012
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.700
Who was that?

c013
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.420
I thought we were alone.

c014
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.720
[unknown voice] I mean it. Put it down.

c015
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.020
-It's not yours.
-We weren't going to.

c016
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.300
[glass shatters]

c017
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.500
What was that?

c018
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.600
Not me.

c019
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.200
That was the jug. Sorry.

c020
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.120
Amara. When did you get in?

c021
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.520
Ten minutes ago. You two were busy.

c022
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.800
Is this yours?

c023
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:38.900
It is.

c024
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.100
What is it?

c025
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.420
I'll tell you when I've opened it.

c026
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.500
So open it.

c027
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.400
Not with you two watching.

c028
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.800
It's definitely hers, then.

c029
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.600
It was never yours.

c030
00:00:50.787 --> 00:00:52.120
It could have been.

c031
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.533
Sweep up the jug.
